{"Header panel ordering may be inverted in flex layout - the refactor removes float and uses margin-left: auto plus order(3), but if other header children don't have matching order values, this can reshuffle header contents and break logo/title/panel alignment": 0.5713424682617188, ".small-action mixes flex and float layout - it's now a flex container while base, desktop, and mobile rules still rely on float/fixed-width/padding layout contracts, causing alignment and spacing to diverge across breakpoints since floats on flex items are ignored": 0.7323359847068787, "order() mixin emits off-by-one value for -webkit-box-ordinal-group - the legacy property is 1-based so order(3) renders as -webkit-box-ordinal-group: 3 which doesn't match modern flexbox ordering semantics and can shift elements by one position in browsers using the 2009 box model": 0.8352675437927246, ".extra-info-wrapper uses order(2) assuming parent is flex container and topic title should sort before it - this creates a stronger contract than old float-based layout where visual order is now dictated by flex ordering not DOM order, potentially reversing or reshuffling elements in responsive variants": 0.5284780263900757}